9
01:15:56,250 --> 01:16:02,250
Moonage Daydream is a 2022 documentary film about English artist David Bowie.

10
01:24:22,500 --> 01:24:28,500
Written, directed, produced and edited by Brett Morgen, the film uses previously
unreleased footage from Bowie's personal archives, including live concert footage.

11
01:32:48,750 --> 01:32:54,750
It is the first film to be officially authorized by Bowie's estate, and
takes its title from the 1972 Bowie song of the same name.

12
01:41:15,000 --> 01:41:21,000
Moonage Daydream had its world premiere at the 2022 Cannes Film
Festival, where it received positive reviews.

13
01:49:41,250 --> 01:49:47,250
It was released theatrically and in IMAX in the
United States on 16 September 2022.

14
01:58:07,500 --> 01:58:13,500
It was shortlisted for Best Documentary Feature at the 95th Academy Awards,
and won Best Music Film at the 66th Annual Grammy Awards.

15
02:06:33,750 --> 02:06:39,750
The film explores themes of rock star, singing,
archive footage, superstar, old footage.
